# Fleet and runtime policy

Before changing fleet bindings, issue dispatch, or tenant provision:

1. Read **`docs/ecosystem/FLEET_AND_RUNTIME_POLICY.md`** (canonical).
2. OpenClaw fleet v1 = five profiles on one gateway; mappings in `LiNKbot/roles/platform/fleet-v1-openclaw.ts`.
3. Agent Zero = eight lanes in `LiNKbot/roles/platform/agent-zero-lanes.ts`.
4. Every issue template MUST declare `runtime_tier` (`automation` | `agent_zero` | `openclaw_head` | `openclaw_subagent` | `codex_lane` | `council`).
5. Tenant isolation is enforced in LiNKaios kernel (`tenant_id` on runs, leases, brain context) — never rely on OpenClaw alone.
6. Legacy LiNKaios UI mappings (`suite-role-mapping.ts`, `openclaw-dispatch.ts`) MUST stay aligned with LiNKbot suite mapping files (Wave 1).

Do not add legacy OpenClaw profile names (`linksites-builder`, `librarian`, `linksuitegen-factory`, etc.) in new code.
